  "bekaa-kafra.html": {
   "- where Youssef Antoun was born, traditionally on May 8, 1828, and grew up the youngest of five. Kept as a place of pilgrimage.": 1,
   "Before the monastery and the hermitage, before the miracles and the crowds, there was a mountain village perched at the top of Lebanon. Youssef Antoun Makhlouf - the boy who would become Saint Charbel - was born here, traditionally on May 8, 1828, and the village has kept his house, his church, and his grotto ever since.": 1,
   "It is the birthplace of Saint Charbel Makhlouf (traditionally May 8, 1828), Lebanon's most beloved saint. His family home, baptism church, and childhood prayer grotto are all preserved there.": 1,
   "Take the Online Tour": 1,
   "Youssef Antoun Makhlouf was born here, traditionally on May 8, 1828, the youngest of five children of Antoun Zaarour Makhlouf and Brigitta Chidiac. His father died when he was about three, and the boy grew up in this house - tending the family's small flock, praying, living the ordinary life of a poor mountain village. The house still stands and is kept as a place of pilgrimage; during the week of Saint Charbel's feast in July, the street leading to it fills with an exhibition of homemade products prepared by the villagers.": 1,
   "About 1,800 meters above sea level - widely known as the highest village in Lebanon - plan for real mountain weather, especially in winter.": 1,
   "Bekaa Kafra, widely known as Lebanon's highest village and Saint Charbel's birthplace: the Makhlouf home, baptism church, prayer grotto, and a complete visiting guide.": 2,
   "The Highest Village in Lebanon": 1,
   "Bekaa Kafra sits at about 1,800 meters above sea level in the Bsharri district of North Lebanon - widely known as the highest village in the country. Its name is Syriac:": 1,
   "In the Bsharri district of North Lebanon, at about 1,800 meters above sea level - widely known as the highest village in Lebanon. It overlooks the Qannoubine valley and neighbors the Cedars of God.": 1
